-- A rule declared in a WHERE is named bare, so it shares an entry with a
-- top-level rule of the same name (overnight card O6, 2026-10-11; found in
-- review). `useOne` calls the top-level `scaled` (rate 3) and `useTwo` its own
-- local `scaled` (rate 5). The rows answer 30, 50 and 80, and every one lists
-- `WITH scaled: rate`.

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
useOne MEANS scaled WITH base IS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
useTwo MEANS scaled WITH base IS n
  WHERE
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 5
          base IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

@export default Combine
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      one IS A BOOLEAN
      two IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS (IF one THEN useOne n ELSE 0) PLUS (IF two THEN useTwo n ELSE 0)
